/-!
# Siegel-set covers of the modular fundamental domain

Definition: `AutomorphicForm_SiegelSetCover` (`fc7b6f84-d9d8-5ae4-addb-5225f537339c`), by Claude,
2026-09-05.

This module records reduction theory for $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ acting on the upper half-plane
$\mathbb{H}$, in the form of height bounds and of covers of $\mathbb{H}$ by translates of Mathlib's
closed fundamental domain $\mathcal{D} = \{\tau : 1 \le |\tau|^2,\ |\operatorname{Re}\tau| \le
1/2\}$. The first group of statements is the height bound: every $\tau \in \mathcal{D}$ satisfies
$\operatorname{Im}\tau \ge \sqrt{3}/2$, and consequently every $z \in \mathbb{H}$ admits $g \in
\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\operatorname{Im}(g \cdot z) \ge \sqrt{3}/2$. The second group
treats an arbitrary subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, not assumed normal, with
$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\Gamma$ the space of cosets and `Quotient.out` the chosen set-theoretic
section: for each $z \in \mathbb{H}$ there are $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and a coset $q$ with
$\mathrm{out}(q) \cdot (\gamma \cdot z) \in \mathcal{D}$, hence also with
$\operatorname{Im}(\mathrm{out}(q)\cdot(\gamma \cdot z)) \ge \sqrt{3}/2$; equivalently, the
$\Gamma$-orbit of $z$ meets $\bigcup_q \mathrm{out}(q)^{-1}\cdot\mathcal{D}$. This is specialised to
$\Gamma = \Gamma_0(N)$ for every natural number $N$, together with the finiteness of
$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\Gamma_0(N)$ for $N \neq 0$, obtained from finiteness of the index, so
that the union above is a finite one.

The remaining statements concern the corner point $\rho = -1/2 + i\sqrt{3}/2$: its imaginary part is
$\sqrt{3}/2$, it lies in $\mathcal{D}$, and for every $g \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ one has
$\operatorname{Im}(g\cdot\rho) \le \sqrt{3}/2$, so the bound $\sqrt{3}/2$ is attained and optimal.
The last fact rests on an auxiliary arithmetic inequality, $c^2 - cd + d^2 \ge 1$ for integers $c,
d$ not both zero, applied to the bottom row of $g$, which computes $|{\cdot}|^2$ of the denominator
$c\rho + d$. Two small further facts are recorded: $1/2 < \sqrt{3}/2$, and $S =
\begin{pmatrix}0&-1\\1&0\end{pmatrix} \notin \Gamma_0(2)$.

**Relation to Mathlib.** No new notions are introduced: $\mathcal{D}$, $\rho$, `Gamma0`, the
denominator $\mathrm{denom}$ and the existence of a translate in $\mathcal{D}$ are Mathlib's, and
the statements here are consequences of Mathlib's reduction theory for $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$
repackaged in the coset form used downstream.

**Where it is used.** The covers and the uniform lower bound $\operatorname{Im} \ge \sqrt{3}/2$ on
suitably translated points serve the analytic side of the modular-forms development, where growth
estimates for automorphic forms are controlled on finitely many translates of the fundamental domain
for $\Gamma_0(N)$.

